&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ad57eac60556d9547d94e96&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Wanqi Yin&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ad57eac60556d9547d94e97&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Hanfei Zhao&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ad57eac60556d9547d94e98&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Tianbo Zhong&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ad57eac60556d9547d94e99&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Long Zhuo&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ad57eac60556d9547d94e9a&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;669f13ed48d82d4a6cfc367b&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/de12931088a3e317633f928c51089c27.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Jing Zuo&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;Panda7777777&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Panda7777777&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Jing Zuo&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-20T16:45:04.602Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false}],&quot;mediaUrls&quot;:[&quot;https://cdn-uploads.huggingface.co/production/uploads/652d06833b5997ed71ce5c46/3Hk2ArDZVOMs0HNqMG5QG.mp4&quot;],&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-15T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Has GPT-6-Astra Achieved Embodied Intelligence?&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;652d06833b5997ed71ce5c46&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/652d06833b5997ed71ce5c46/O_D6bpa5mGxLA7uCjmVCG.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Zhongang Cai&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;caizhongang&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;caizhongang&quot;},&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;GPT-6-Astra demonstrates a level of competence in robotic manipulation and navigation that challenges the conventional paradigm of building specialized models for individual tasks and embodiments. In this report, we ask not only how capable GPT-6-Astra is, but what its capabilities imply for the field. First, we probe the limits of standalone GPT-6-Astra. We conduct a large-scale evaluation across 12 representative benchmarks spanning tabletop manipulation, humanoids, mobile platforms, and dexterous hands. Under a unified protocol that allows in-context learning (ICL) from training-set demonstrations and substantially increases the number of execution steps, GPT-6-Astra achieves unprecedented performance (Fig. 1). Future research may focus on improving 1) the generality of ICL 2) cost and execution time, 3) physical-state verification, 4) recovery from irreversible failures, and 5) long-horizon preservation of progress. Second, we study the agentic harness for embodied control. We identify that close-loop coordination between a high-level \&quot;System 2\&quot; reasoner (i.e., GPT-6-Astra) and a low-level \&quot;System 1\&quot; controller (e.g., π0.5) is costly but effective. Third, we examine GPT-6-Astra on real-world deployment. Our experiments on 8 robot configurations reveal substantial gaps: 1) robot demonstrations required for ICL are expensive to collect, and 2) it is implausible to trade longer execution for higher success rates with physical constraints. Fourth, we envision the next generation of embodied benchmarks. We develop a prototype that 1) derives tasks from real-world needs, 2) provides no in-domain demonstrations, and 3) judges agents on a world clock that keeps running while they deliberate. Taken together, our results suggest that GPT-6-Astra has largely crossed the threshold of embodied competence, but not yet that of practical embodied intelligence.&quot;,&quot;upvotes&quot;:135,&quot;discussionId&quot;:&quot;6ad57eac60556d9547d94e9b&quot;,&quot;projectPage&quot;:&quot;https://sensenova.ai/has-gpt-6-astra-achieved-embodied-intelligence&quot;,&quot;githubRepo&quot;:&quot;https://github.com/OpenSenseNova/SenseNova-RoboRSI&quot;,&quot;githubRepoAddedBy&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;ai_summary&quot;:&quot;GPT-6-Astra achieves high performance across diverse robotic tasks via in-context learning, yet real-world deployment reveals gaps in demonstration cost, execution time, and practical embodied intelligence.&quot;,&quot;ai_keywords&quot;:[&quot;in-context learning&quot;,&quot;System 2 reasoner&quot;,&quot;System 1 controller&quot;,&quot;close-loop coordination&quot;,&quot;embodied control&quot;,&quot;long-horizon preservation&quot;,&quot;physical-state verification&quot;],&quot;ai_summary_model&quot;:&quot;thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small&quot;,&quot;githubStars&quot;:516,&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;64f0405f8a4cf3e5e6b38f9c&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;sensenova&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;SenseNova&quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/652d06833b5997ed71ce5c46/k66xcOMf4NVbMSFulUjHY.png&quot;}},&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-14T20:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Has GPT-6-Astra Achieved Embodied Intelligence?&quot;,&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;GPT-6-Astra demonstrates a level of competence in robotic manipulation and navigation that challenges the conventional paradigm of building specialized models for individual tasks and embodiments. In this report, we ask not only how capable GPT-6-Astra is, but what its capabilities imply for the field. First, we probe the limits of standalone GPT-6-Astra. We conduct a large-scale evaluation across 12 representative benchmarks spanning tabletop manipulation, humanoids, mobile platforms, and dexterous hands. Under a unified protocol that allows in-context learning (ICL) from training-set demonstrations and substantially increases the number of execution steps, GPT-6-Astra achieves unprecedented performance (Fig. 1). Future research may focus on improving 1) the generality of ICL 2) cost and execution time, 3) physical-state verification, 4) recovery from irreversible failures, and 5) long-horizon preservation of progress. Second, we study the agentic harness for embodied control. We identify that close-loop coordination between a high-level \&quot;System 2\&quot; reasoner (i.e., GPT-6-Astra) and a low-level \&quot;System 1\&quot; controller (e.g., π0.5) is costly but effective. Third, we examine GPT-6-Astra on real-world deployment. Our experiments on 8 robot configurations reveal substantial gaps: 1) robot demonstrations required for ICL are expensive to collect, and 2) it is implausible to trade longer execution for higher success rates with physical constraints. Fourth, we envision the next generation of embodied benchmarks. We develop a prototype that 1) derives tasks from real-world needs, 2) provides no in-domain demonstrations, and 3) judges agents on a world clock that keeps running while they deliberate. Taken together, our results suggest that GPT-6-Astra has largely crossed the threshold of embodied competence, but not yet that of practical embodied intelligence.&quot;,&quot;mediaUrls&quot;:[&quot;https://cdn-uploads.huggingface.co/production/uploads/652d06833b5997ed71ce5c46/3Hk2ArDZVOMs0HNqMG5QG.mp4&quot;],&quot;thumbnail&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-thumbnails.huggingface.co/social-thumbnails/papers/2610.22471.png&quot;,&quot;numComments&quot;:2,&quot;upvoted&quot;:false,&quot;submittedBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;652d06833b5997ed71ce5c46&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/652d06833b5997ed71ce5c46/O_D6bpa5mGxLA7uCjmVCG.jpeg&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Zhongang Cai&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;caizhongang&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;isHf&quot;:false,&quot;isHfAdmin&quot;:false,&quot;isMod&quot;:false,&quot;followerCount&quot;:47,&quot;isUserFollowing&quot;:false},&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;64f0405f8a4cf3e5e6b38f9c&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;sensenova&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;SenseNova&quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/652d06833b5997ed71ce5c46/k66xcOMf4NVbMSFulUjHY.png&quot;},&quot;isAuthorParticipating&quot;:true},{&quot;paper&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;2606.03748&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:[{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6a1f9080e292c1c78ecb132f&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Glenn Jocher&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6a1f9080e292c1c78ecb1330&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Jing Qiu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6a1f9080e292c1c78ecb1331&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Mengyu Liu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6a1f9080e292c1c78ecb1332&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Shuai Lyu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6a1f9080e292c1c78ecb1333&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;617e7dbd129c9e67703ffe62&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/617e7dbd129c9e67703ffe62/nJD_rI351t2c2QN_BpUBz.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Fatih C. Akyon&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;fcakyon&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;fcakyon&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Fatih Cagatay Akyon&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-06-09T12:47:21.531Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6a1f9080e292c1c78ecb1334&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Muhammet Esat Kalfaoglu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false}],&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-06-02T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyAt&quot;:&quot;2026-06-03T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Ultralytics YOLO26: Unified Real-Time End-to-End Vision Models&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;5f1158120c833276f61f1a84&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/1608042047613-5f1158120c833276f61f1a84.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Niels Rogge&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;nielsr&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;nielsr&quot;},&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;Real-time vision demands models that are accurate, efficient, and simple to deploy across diverse hardware. The YOLO family has become widely deployed for this reason, yet most YOLO detectors still rely on non-maximum suppression at inference, carry heavy detection heads due to Distribution Focal Loss, require long training schedules, and can leave the smallest objects without positive label assignments. We present Ultralytics YOLO26, a unified real-time vision model family that addresses these limitations through coordinated architecture and training advances. YOLO26 uses a dual-head design for native NMS-free end-to-end inference and removes DFL entirely, yielding a lighter head with unconstrained regression range. Its training pipeline combines MuSGD, a hybrid Muon-SGD optimizer adapted from large language model training; Progressive Loss, which shifts supervision toward the inference-time head; and STAL, a label assignment strategy that guarantees positive coverage for small objects. Beyond detection, YOLO26 introduces task-specific head and loss designs for instance segmentation, pose estimation, and oriented detection, producing consistent gains across tasks and scales. The family spans five scales (n/s/m/l/x) and supports detection, instance segmentation, pose estimation, classification, and oriented detection in a single pipeline, with an open-vocabulary extension, YOLOE-26, for text-, visual-, and prompt-free inference. Across all scales, YOLO26 achieves 40.9-57.5 mAP on COCO at 1.7-11.8 ms T4 TensorRT latency, advancing the accuracy-latency Pareto front over prior real-time detectors, while YOLOE-26x reaches 40.6 AP on LVIS minival under text prompting. Code and models are available at https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics.&quot;,&quot;upvotes&quot;:25,&quot;discussionId&quot;:&quot;6a1f9080e292c1c78ecb1335&quot;,&quot;projectPage&quot;:&quot;https://docs.ultralytics.com/models/yolo26&quot;,&quot;githubRepo&quot;:&quot;https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics&quot;,&quot;githubRepoAddedBy&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;ai_summary&quot;:&quot;YOLO26 addresses real-time vision challenges through a unified model family with NMS-free inference, improved training strategies, and multi-task capabilities spanning detection, segmentation, and pose estimation.&quot;,&quot;ai_keywords&quot;:[&quot;YOLO&quot;,&quot;non-maximum suppression&quot;,&quot;Distribution Focal Loss&quot;,&quot;MuSGD&quot;,&quot;hybrid Muon-SGD optimizer&quot;,&quot;Progressive Loss&quot;,&quot;STAL&quot;,&quot;instance segmentation&quot;,&quot;pose estimation&quot;,&quot;oriented detection&quot;,&quot;open-vocabulary extension&quot;,&quot;TensorRT latency&quot;,&quot;mAP&quot;,&quot;COCO&quot;,&quot;LVIS&quot;],&quot;ai_summary_model&quot;:&quot;Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct&quot;,&quot;githubStars&quot;:63205,&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;65ba54e4b6b3191a83624cee&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ultralytics&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Ultralytics&quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/60ad037a306d6873ec42d537/iusy6Ia8JeCK-ui4z-kjE.png&quot;}},&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-06-01T20:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Ultralytics YOLO26: Unified Real-Time End-to-End Vision Models&quot;,&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;Real-time vision demands models that are accurate, efficient, and simple to deploy across diverse hardware. The YOLO family has become widely deployed for this reason, yet most YOLO detectors still rely on non-maximum suppression at inference, carry heavy detection heads due to Distribution Focal Loss, require long training schedules, and can leave the smallest objects without positive label assignments. We present Ultralytics YOLO26, a unified real-time vision model family that addresses these limitations through coordinated architecture and training advances. YOLO26 uses a dual-head design for native NMS-free end-to-end inference and removes DFL entirely, yielding a lighter head with unconstrained regression range. Its training pipeline combines MuSGD, a hybrid Muon-SGD optimizer adapted from large language model training; Progressive Loss, which shifts supervision toward the inference-time head; and STAL, a label assignment strategy that guarantees positive coverage for small objects. Beyond detection, YOLO26 introduces task-specific head and loss designs for instance segmentation, pose estimation, and oriented detection, producing consistent gains across tasks and scales. The family spans five scales (n/s/m/l/x) and supports detection, instance segmentation, pose estimation, classification, and oriented detection in a single pipeline, with an open-vocabulary extension, YOLOE-26, for text-, visual-, and prompt-free inference. Across all scales, YOLO26 achieves 40.9-57.5 mAP on COCO at 1.7-11.8 ms T4 TensorRT latency, advancing the accuracy-latency Pareto front over prior real-time detectors, while YOLOE-26x reaches 40.6 AP on LVIS minival under text prompting. Code and models are available at https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics.&quot;,&quot;thumbnail&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-thumbnails.huggingface.co/social-thumbnails/papers/2606.03748.png&quot;,&quot;numComments&quot;:1,&quot;upvoted&quot;:false,&quot;submittedBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;5f1158120c833276f61f1a84&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/1608042047613-5f1158120c833276f61f1a84.jpeg&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Niels Rogge&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;nielsr&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;isHf&quot;:true,&quot;isHfAdmin&quot;:false,&quot;isMod&quot;:false,&quot;followerCount&quot;:1364,&quot;isUserFollowing&quot;:false},&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;65ba54e4b6b3191a83624cee&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ultralytics&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Ultralytics&quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/60ad037a306d6873ec42d537/iusy6Ia8JeCK-ui4z-kjE.png&quot;},&quot;isAuthorParticipating&quot;:false},{&quot;paper&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;2611.03126&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:[{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a80b&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;67d63e228d5c7a132cbcf39b&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/no-auth/ynwA3Sya5irwMRCmSeLiC.png&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;neil yu&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;yxl66666&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;yxl66666&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Xinlei Yu&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-11-04T20:33:40.303Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a80c&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Gen Li&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a80d&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ji Zhao&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a80e&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zhangquan Chen&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a80f&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Congcong Wang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a810&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;66e02f04ec26df895d24e86a&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/no-auth/NgRs6uIChjP8_fpxw_3p-.png&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;dong&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;shuai22&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;shuai22&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Shuai Dong&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-11-05T11:34:35.189Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a811&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zelin Peng&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a812&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Yuqi Xu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a813&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Hongrui Wu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a814&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Kaiwen Tuo&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a815&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Cheng Yang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a816&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Kaituo Feng&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a817&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Yifan Wu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a818&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Jiayi Zhang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a819&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Dongming Wu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a81a&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Wenqi Shao&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a81b&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Jiaqi Wang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a81c&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Xiangyu Yue&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false}],&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-11-02T13:41:14.000Z&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyAt&quot;:&quot;2026-11-03T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;CUA-Master: Scaling Computer-use Agents through Open-World Recursive Improvements&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;67d63e228d5c7a132cbcf39b&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/no-auth/ynwA3Sya5irwMRCmSeLiC.png&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;neil yu&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;yxl66666&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;yxl66666&quot;},&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;Despite recent advances in CUAs, their development remains constrained by the limited diversity, controllability, and reliability of interaction data. Moreover, conventional optimization pipelines lack iterative feedback, while existing recursive improvement approaches often rely on self-generated experiences, limiting ability expansion and yielding diminishing returns. To address these challenges, we introduce CUA-Master, a nested double-loop recursive improvement framework. At the system level, an outer world-data-model flywheel continuously incorporates open-world corpus and leverages evolving model weaknesses to guide subsequent data construction and optimization iterations. At the data level, an inner flywheel couples open-world seeding and autocatalytic propagation. The former mines authentic workflows as seed tasks from instructional videos, and employs visual-semantic dual-path trajectory reconstruction; The latter transforms these seeds into reusable primitives for controllable synthesis of diverse, complex, and verifiable tasks. To enable efficient and reliable trajectory collection, we further introduce a feedback-guided snapshot-rollback retry mechanism in various real environments. Extensive experiments demonstrate that CUA-Master-27B achieves competitive performance across GUI-only and GUI-CLI hybrid benchmarks, scoring 80.2 on OSWorld Verified, 36.9 on OSWorld 2.0, 43.9 on WeaveBench, and 25.0 on Agents' Last Exam. Our framework also substantially improves the quality and efficiency of data synthesis, and exhibits continuous gains across recursive iterations.&quot;,&quot;upvotes&quot;:46,&quot;discussionId&quot;:&quot;6ae97cf94b63b3479c38a81d&quot;,&quot;projectPage&quot;:&quot;https://xlyu0106.github.io/CUA-Master/&quot;,&quot;githubRepo&quot;:&quot;https://github.com/xlyu0106/CUA-Master&quot;,&quot;githubRepoAddedBy&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;ai_summary&quot;:&quot;CUA-Master uses nested recursive loops with open-world data and feedback-driven retries to continuously improve computer-use agents across diverse benchmarks.&quot;,&quot;ai_keywords&quot;:[&quot;CUA-Master&quot;,&quot;nested double-loop recursive improvement&quot;,&quot;world-data-model flywheel&quot;,&quot;open-world corpus&quot;,&quot;visual-semantic dual-path trajectory reconstruction&quot;,&quot;autocatalytic propagation&quot;,&quot;reusable primitives&quot;,&quot;feedback-guided snapshot-rollback retry&quot;,&quot;GUI-CLI hybrid benchmarks&quot;],&quot;ai_summary_model&quot;:&quot;thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small&quot;,&quot;githubStars&quot;:124},&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-11-02T08:41:14.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;CUA-Master: Scaling Computer-use Agents through Open-World Recursive Improvements&quot;,&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;Despite recent advances in CUAs, their development remains constrained by the limited diversity, controllability, and reliability of interaction data. Moreover, conventional optimization pipelines lack iterative feedback, while existing recursive improvement approaches often rely on self-generated experiences, limiting ability expansion and yielding diminishing returns. To address these challenges, we introduce CUA-Master, a nested double-loop recursive improvement framework. At the system level, an outer world-data-model flywheel continuously incorporates open-world corpus and leverages evolving model weaknesses to guide subsequent data construction and optimization iterations. At the data level, an inner flywheel couples open-world seeding and autocatalytic propagation. The former mines authentic workflows as seed tasks from instructional videos, and employs visual-semantic dual-path trajectory reconstruction; The latter transforms these seeds into reusable primitives for controllable synthesis of diverse, complex, and verifiable tasks. To enable efficient and reliable trajectory collection, we further introduce a feedback-guided snapshot-rollback retry mechanism in various real environments. Extensive experiments demonstrate that CUA-Master-27B achieves competitive performance across GUI-only and GUI-CLI hybrid benchmarks, scoring 80.2 on OSWorld Verified, 36.9 on OSWorld 2.0, 43.9 on WeaveBench, and 25.0 on Agents' Last Exam. Our framework also substantially improves the quality and efficiency of data synthesis, and exhibits continuous gains across recursive iterations.&quot;,&quot;thumbnail&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-thumbnails.huggingface.co/social-thumbnails/papers/2611.03126.png&quot;,&quot;numComments&quot;:2,&quot;upvoted&quot;:false,&quot;submittedBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;67d63e228d5c7a132cbcf39b&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/no-auth/ynwA3Sya5irwMRCmSeLiC.png&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;neil yu&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;yxl66666&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;isHf&quot;:false,&quot;isHfAdmin&quot;:false,&quot;isMod&quot;:false,&quot;followerCount&quot;:4,&quot;isUserFollowing&quot;:false},&quot;isAuthorParticipating&quot;:true},{&quot;paper&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;2609.38839&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:[{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ac30e225c93eba55d4df0f6&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;647dd8f9a49bffab5d6fe46e&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/no-auth/UkYcsNfnvKOotfKfTNcEk.png&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Yin Bo&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;YINBO0927&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;YINBO0927&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Bo Yin&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-05T16:45:05.343Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ac30e225c93eba55d4df0f7&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Xiaobin Hu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ac30e225c93eba55d4df0f8&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6561d33d462e5ebcbffb8bc3&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/5e57e611e69d3a4d9485614cd6fb216d.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Jiaqi Zhao&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;zjq0455&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;zjq0455&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Jiaqi Zhao&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-05T16:45:05.352Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ac30e225c93eba55d4df0f9&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Shuicheng Yan&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false}],&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-05T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;FrameMorrow: Future-guided Frame Selection with Prospective Tokens for Long-Horizon Video Generation&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;647dd8f9a49bffab5d6fe46e&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/no-auth/UkYcsNfnvKOotfKfTNcEk.png&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Yin Bo&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;YINBO0927&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;YINBO0927&quot;},&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;Long-horizon video generation requires models to effectively leverage an increasingly long generation history. As the generated history grows, retaining all previous content becomes increasingly expensive and redundant, making effective historical selection essential. Existing approaches often determine historical relevance based on the current content. However, information relevant to the present is not necessarily useful for future generation, while seemingly less relevant history may become important later. Our key insight is that historical information should be selected according to its relevance to future information needs. Capturing these needs does not require generating the full future; instead, a compact representation of what becomes important next is sufficient to guide historical selection. Building on this insight, we propose FrameMorrow, a prospective frame selector that predicts a small set of prospective tokens representing future information needs and uses them to identify relevant information from history. FrameMorrow selects explicit historical frames rather than model-specific internal states, enabling plug-and-play integration across diverse generators, including closed-source models, with little additional inference cost. We evaluate FrameMorrow across five benchmarks and 11 generative models spanning long-video generation, interactive generation, and action-conditioned world models. Extensive experiments demonstrate consistent improvements in long-range consistency, visual quality, and action alignment across diverse generation settings.&quot;,&quot;upvotes&quot;:49,&quot;discussionId&quot;:&quot;6ac30e225c93eba55d4df0fa&quot;,&quot;projectPage&quot;:&quot;https://yinbo0927.github.io/FrameMorrow/&quot;,&quot;githubRepo&quot;:&quot;https://github.com/YinBo0927/FrameMorrow&quot;,&quot;githubRepoAddedBy&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;ai_summary&quot;:&quot;FrameMorrow improves long-horizon video generation by selecting historical frames based on predicted future information needs rather than current content.&quot;,&quot;ai_keywords&quot;:[&quot;prospective frame selector&quot;,&quot;prospective tokens&quot;,&quot;historical selection&quot;,&quot;long-horizon video generation&quot;,&quot;plug-and-play integration&quot;,&quot;closed-source models&quot;,&quot;long-range consistency&quot;],&quot;ai_summary_model&quot;:&quot;thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small&quot;,&quot;githubStars&quot;:230,&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6508ab2b349930913196378b&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;NationalUniversityofSingapore&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;National University of Singapore&quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/630ca0817dacb93b33506ce7/ZYUmpSMsa5Whihw3me2Bw.png&quot;}},&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-09-29T20:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;FrameMorrow: Future-guided Frame Selection with Prospective Tokens for Long-Horizon Video Generation&quot;,&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;Long-horizon video generation requires models to effectively leverage an increasingly long generation history. As the generated history grows, retaining all previous content becomes increasingly expensive and redundant, making effective historical selection essential. Existing approaches often determine historical relevance based on the current content. However, information relevant to the present is not necessarily useful for future generation, while seemingly less relevant history may become important later. Our key insight is that historical information should be selected according to its relevance to future information needs. Capturing these needs does not require generating the full future; instead, a compact representation of what becomes important next is sufficient to guide historical selection. Building on this insight, we propose FrameMorrow, a prospective frame selector that predicts a small set of prospective tokens representing future information needs and uses them to identify relevant information from history. FrameMorrow selects explicit historical frames rather than model-specific internal states, enabling plug-and-play integration across diverse generators, including closed-source models, with little additional inference cost. We evaluate FrameMorrow across five benchmarks and 11 generative models spanning long-video generation, interactive generation, and action-conditioned world models. Extensive experiments demonstrate consistent improvements in long-range consistency, visual quality, and action alignment across diverse generation settings.&quot;,&quot;thumbnail&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-thumbnails.huggingface.co/social-thumbnails/papers/2609.38839.png&quot;,&quot;numComments&quot;:4,&quot;upvoted&quot;:false,&quot;submittedBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;647dd8f9a49bffab5d6fe46e&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/no-auth/UkYcsNfnvKOotfKfTNcEk.png&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Yin Bo&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;YINBO0927&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;isHf&quot;:false,&quot;isHfAdmin&quot;:false,&quot;isMod&quot;:false,&quot;followerCount&quot;:1,&quot;isUserFollowing&quot;:false},&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6508ab2b349930913196378b&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;NationalUniversityofSingapore&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;National University of Singapore&quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/630ca0817dacb93b33506ce7/ZYUmpSMsa5Whihw3me2Bw.png&quot;},&quot;isAuthorParticipating&quot;:true},{&quot;paper&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;2610.22352&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:[{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ad1da588304c5d882d7ba37&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6acf884afae2645be6242d8c&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/18fd2a1cfcf28554ee35b13447790e34.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;chen flank&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;supra3d&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;supra3d&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Chen Yang&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-16T08:28:53.296Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ad1da588304c5d882d7ba38&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;652cf49cc6857682d3168f5a&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/7087ea6897942f2f6b822b1587ce1248.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Jiemin Fang&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;JieminFang&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;JieminFang&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Jiemin Fang&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-16T16:45:05.465Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ad1da588304c5d882d7ba39&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;652ba501802e3d1a4fc087fa&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/35c378cf709ede1dc124a4762a1442ab.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Fanpeng Meng&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;fpmeng01&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;fpmeng01&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Fanpeng Meng&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-27T08:45:04.778Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ad1da588304c5d882d7ba3a&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;631b24f2f6bc4be4a64c4d43&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/631b24f2f6bc4be4a64c4d43/P9_tVF7SESmVxxGKVCgCk.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Zihao Huang&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;Inso&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Inso&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zihao Huang&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-16T16:45:05.471Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ad1da588304c5d882d7ba3b&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Jichen Pang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ad1da588304c5d882d7ba3c&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Guanjun Wu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ad1da588304c5d882d7ba3d&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zhikuan Bao&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ad1da588304c5d882d7ba3e&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Qi Tian&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false}],&quot;mediaUrls&quot;:[&quot;https://cdn-uploads.huggingface.co/production/uploads/6acf884afae2645be6242d8c/5SrSnwdmCeTwQU9MAzJEo.mp4&quot;],&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-15T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;SUPRA-TEX: 3D Generation with Super-Aligned Texture&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6acf884afae2645be6242d8c&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/18fd2a1cfcf28554ee35b13447790e34.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;chen flank&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;supra3d&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;supra3d&quot;},&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;Single image 3D generation aims to dress a given 3D mesh with relightable materials while faithfully preserving the visual details of a reference image. Existing methods either introduce artifacts when fusing inconsistent multi-view predictions or struggle to preserve fine details through implicit image-feature conditioning. To resolve these challenges, we introduce SUPRA-Tex, built on the principle of decoupling visible-material estimation, surface alignment, and observation-guided 3D completion. This division of labor allows the 3D generator, trained on limited 3D data, to focus its capacity on preserving visible evidence and completing unobserved surfaces. Specifically, we first train an MLLM-based image editing model to predict lighting-separated PBR maps in the reference view. We then project these maps onto the visible surface and encode them with the pretrained material VAE encoder into native observation latents that share the generation target's latent space. An interleaved flow transformer holds these latents as fixed, read-only anchors while alternating unobserved-region and full-surface updates to generate complete material latents. This design achieves super-alignment with the reference, delivering What You See Is What You Get fidelity on visible regions and coherent completion on unobserved surfaces. Trained solely on public datasets, SUPRA-Tex achieves SOTA performance in both geometry-conditioned texturing and end-to-end asset generation, matching or even exceeding leading commercial systems on in-the-wild images. Project page: https://supra-3d.github.io/supratex/&quot;,&quot;upvotes&quot;:13,&quot;discussionId&quot;:&quot;6ad1da598304c5d882d7ba3f&quot;,&quot;projectPage&quot;:&quot;https://supra-3d.github.io/supratex/&quot;,&quot;githubRepo&quot;:&quot;https://github.com/Supra-3D/SUPRA-Tex&quot;,&quot;githubRepoAddedBy&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;ai_summary&quot;:&quot;SUPRA-Tex decouples visible-material estimation, surface alignment, and 3D completion to generate relightable 3D materials that preserve reference image details and complete unobserved surfaces.&quot;,&quot;ai_keywords&quot;:[&quot;single image 3D generation&quot;,&quot;PBR maps&quot;,&quot;MLLM-based image editing&quot;,&quot;material VAE encoder&quot;,&quot;observation latents&quot;,&quot;interleaved flow transformer&quot;,&quot;geometry-conditioned texturing&quot;],&quot;ai_summary_model&quot;:&quot;thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small&quot;,&quot;githubStars&quot;:707},&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-14T20:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;SUPRA-TEX: 3D Generation with Super-Aligned Texture&quot;,&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;Single image 3D generation aims to dress a given 3D mesh with relightable materials while faithfully preserving the visual details of a reference image. Existing methods either introduce artifacts when fusing inconsistent multi-view predictions or struggle to preserve fine details through implicit image-feature conditioning. To resolve these challenges, we introduce SUPRA-Tex, built on the principle of decoupling visible-material estimation, surface alignment, and observation-guided 3D completion. This division of labor allows the 3D generator, trained on limited 3D data, to focus its capacity on preserving visible evidence and completing unobserved surfaces. Specifically, we first train an MLLM-based image editing model to predict lighting-separated PBR maps in the reference view. We then project these maps onto the visible surface and encode them with the pretrained material VAE encoder into native observation latents that share the generation target's latent space. An interleaved flow transformer holds these latents as fixed, read-only anchors while alternating unobserved-region and full-surface updates to generate complete material latents. This design achieves super-alignment with the reference, delivering What You See Is What You Get fidelity on visible regions and coherent completion on unobserved surfaces. Trained solely on public datasets, SUPRA-Tex achieves SOTA performance in both geometry-conditioned texturing and end-to-end asset generation, matching or even exceeding leading commercial systems on in-the-wild images. Project page: https://supra-3d.github.io/supratex/&quot;,&quot;mediaUrls&quot;:[&quot;https://cdn-uploads.huggingface.co/production/uploads/6acf884afae2645be6242d8c/5SrSnwdmCeTwQU9MAzJEo.mp4&quot;],&quot;thumbnail&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-thumbnails.huggingface.co/social-thumbnails/papers/2610.22352.png&quot;,&quot;numComments&quot;:2,&quot;upvoted&quot;:false,&quot;submittedBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6acf884afae2645be6242d8c&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/18fd2a1cfcf28554ee35b13447790e34.svg&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;chen flank&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;supra3d&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;isHf&quot;:false,&quot;isHfAdmin&quot;:false,&quot;isMod&quot;:false,&quot;followerCount&quot;:2,&quot;isUserFollowing&quot;:false},&quot;isAuthorParticipating&quot;:true},{&quot;paper&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;2611.06518&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:[{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adaa&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Mingzhe Zheng&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adab&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Yue Wu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adac&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Jing Tan&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adad&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Chang Zou&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adae&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Dengyang Jiang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adaf&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zeyue Tian&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adb0&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Xuanhua He&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adb1&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ryan Xu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adb2&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Yunyang Ge&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adb3&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Sihui Ji&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adb4&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;64ecb174f22081b4ac7ca397&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/64ecb174f22081b4ac7ca397/PiAPtD_rbuhGOqfE6ZSIu.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Yunlong Lin&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;LYL1015&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;LYL1015&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Yunlong Lin&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-11-05T08:45:05.136Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adb5&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Kaihang Pan&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adb6&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Hongru Yan&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adb7&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Sixiang Chen&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adb8&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Dianyi Wang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adb9&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Julian Zhang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adba&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Weijie Kong&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adbb&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Changlin Li&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adbc&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Lanqing Guo&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adbd&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zhao Zhong&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adbe&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Qifeng Chen&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adbf&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Harry Yang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false}],&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-11-04T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyAt&quot;:&quot;2026-11-05T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;EmoReward: Self-Evolving Reward Calibration for Emotional Video Generation RL&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;62f0c4abe2999b231e5a893c&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/6bc9047ab569d4c82845efeb663cf65a.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Mingzhe Zheng&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;Dunge0nMaster&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Dunge0nMaster&quot;},&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) has advanced generative model post-training in verifiable domains such as code and mathematics, but evaluating video quality, especially emotional expression, often depends on subjective aesthetics and has no uniquely correct target. Existing approaches typically rely on fixed rewards for visual quality, motion quality, and text alignment that poorly capture emotional intent and can invite reward hacking, while RLHF is difficult to scale and subject to individual aesthetic differences that complicate the calibration of facial, body motion, and chromatic cues across narrative contexts. We introduce EmoReward, a new self-evolving training mechanism that distills evidence reliability from reward traces collected during an actual training run to adaptively guide multi-reward weight allocation in subsequent training by determining which emotional evidence to trust and how much to weight it. EmoReward first plans specific grounding cues from the emotional prompt to guide evaluation, then uses heterogeneous signal primitives to score the generated video during the act stage. Reflective Reward Gating calibrates their contributions through instance-level gates for phase, face confidence, conflict, and subtlety, then renormalizes weights over the active set to produce the sample's fused reward. RewardMemory then estimates each primitive's reliability from rollout scores and outcomes within each emotional regime in the finished training run, then fixes bounded multipliers that calibrate fusion weights in the next training run without updating reward models. Experiments on HunyuanVideo 1.5 show improvements across multiple RL algorithms and compare EmoReward with other agentic reward methods under SAGE-GRPO. Ablations and transfer experiments on SD 3.5 and FLUX further support adaptive reward calibration for visual generation.&quot;,&quot;upvotes&quot;:25,&quot;discussionId&quot;:&quot;6aec221d870269964d13adc0&quot;,&quot;projectPage&quot;:&quot;https://emoreward-project.github.io/&quot;,&quot;githubRepo&quot;:&quot;https://github.com/Tencent-Hunyuan/EmoReward&quot;,&quot;githubRepoAddedBy&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;githubStars&quot;:37,&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6645f953c39288df638dbdd5&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Tencent-Hunyuan&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Tencent Hunyuan&quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/62d22496c58f969c152bcefd/woKSjt2wXvBNKussyYPsa.png&quot;}},&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-11-03T19:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;EmoReward: Self-Evolving Reward Calibration for Emotional Video Generation RL&quot;,&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) has advanced generative model post-training in verifiable domains such as code and mathematics, but evaluating video quality, especially emotional expression, often depends on subjective aesthetics and has no uniquely correct target. Existing approaches typically rely on fixed rewards for visual quality, motion quality, and text alignment that poorly capture emotional intent and can invite reward hacking, while RLHF is difficult to scale and subject to individual aesthetic differences that complicate the calibration of facial, body motion, and chromatic cues across narrative contexts. We introduce EmoReward, a new self-evolving training mechanism that distills evidence reliability from reward traces collected during an actual training run to adaptively guide multi-reward weight allocation in subsequent training by determining which emotional evidence to trust and how much to weight it. EmoReward first plans specific grounding cues from the emotional prompt to guide evaluation, then uses heterogeneous signal primitives to score the generated video during the act stage. Reflective Reward Gating calibrates their contributions through instance-level gates for phase, face confidence, conflict, and subtlety, then renormalizes weights over the active set to produce the sample's fused reward. RewardMemory then estimates each primitive's reliability from rollout scores and outcomes within each emotional regime in the finished training run, then fixes bounded multipliers that calibrate fusion weights in the next training run without updating reward models. Experiments on HunyuanVideo 1.5 show improvements across multiple RL algorithms and compare EmoReward with other agentic reward methods under SAGE-GRPO. Ablations and transfer experiments on SD 3.5 and FLUX further support adaptive reward calibration for visual generation.&quot;,&quot;thumbnail&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-thumbnails.huggingface.co/social-thumbnails/papers/2611.06518.png&quot;,&quot;numComments&quot;:2,&quot;upvoted&quot;:false,&quot;submittedBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;62f0c4abe2999b231e5a893c&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/6bc9047ab569d4c82845efeb663cf65a.svg&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Mingzhe Zheng&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Dunge0nMaster&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;isHf&quot;:false,&quot;isHfAdmin&quot;:false,&quot;isMod&quot;:false,&quot;followerCount&quot;:2,&quot;isUserFollowing&quot;:false},&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6645f953c39288df638dbdd5&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Tencent-Hunyuan&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Tencent Hunyuan&quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/62d22496c58f969c152bcefd/woKSjt2wXvBNKussyYPsa.png&quot;},&quot;isAuthorParticipating&quot;:false},{&quot;paper&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;2603.26164&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:[{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dbc&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6751a4fedf636b0140a9b873&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/b51346e5a6104cd99f12b8f66b6adadc.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:true,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Hao Liang&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;lhpku20010120&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;lhpku20010120&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Hao Liang&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-04-03T09:08:55.763Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dbd&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zhengyang Zhao&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dbe&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Meiyi Qiang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dbf&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;64049e1d0ab5e22719f37be2&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/37d24b50b5a960a03eaf0a4091b99535.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Mingrui Chen&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;Walnutes&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Walnutes&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Mingrui Chen&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-04-07T08:46:44.977Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dc0&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Lu Ma&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dc1&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Rongyi Yu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dc2&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Hengyi Feng&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dc3&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Shixuan Sun&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dc4&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zimo Meng&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dc5&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;65099d08f37afbab0d3fb268&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/1bd467840b6372d167141d5aeba71478.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Xiaochen Ma&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;Sunnyhaze&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Sunnyhaze&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Xiaochen Ma&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-04-10T07:45:25.046Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dc6&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Xuanlin Yang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dc7&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Qifeng Cai&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dc8&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ruichuan An&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dc9&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6671214c92412fd4640714eb&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/c1556168b703c9b87276fb679d044f61.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Bohan Zeng&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;zbhpku&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;zbhpku&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Bohan Zeng&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-04-07T08:46:42.874Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dca&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;65d3149f0545ab7c11568b2b&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/b11ef46f9337085076c35de055005399.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Zhen Hao Wong&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;aaron1141&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;aaron1141&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zhen Hao Wong&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-07-28T08:45:04.408Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dcb&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Chengyu Shen&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dcc&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;65b7098af327f1f4e315294d&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/65b7098af327f1f4e315294d/38JtHebJ_XYWciMA15vJ3.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Runming He&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;blackBOX25I47&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;blackBOX25I47&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Runming He&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-07-22T07:39:29.120Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dcd&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zhaoyang Han&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dce&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;642fef28a043f0ac7defa8a9&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/642fef28a043f0ac7defa8a9/RwOEkuj3fOnOA54tGR7Ea.png&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Yaowei Zheng&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;hiyouga&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;hiyouga&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Yaowei Zheng&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-08-06T16:45:04.371Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dcf&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Fangcheng Fu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dd0&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Conghui He&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dd1&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Bin Cui&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dd2&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zhiyu Li&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dd3&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Weinan E&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dd4&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Wentao Zhang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false}],&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-03-27T08:28:02.000Z&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyAt&quot;:&quot;2026-04-03T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;DataFlex: A Unified Framework for Data-Centric Dynamic Training of Large Language Models&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6671214c92412fd4640714eb&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/c1556168b703c9b87276fb679d044f61.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Bohan Zeng&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;zbhpku&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;zbhpku&quot;},&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;Data-centric training has emerged as a promising direction for improving large language models (LLMs) by optimizing not only model parameters but also the selection, composition, and weighting of training data during optimization. However, existing approaches to data selection, data mixture optimization, and data reweighting are often developed in isolated codebases with inconsistent interfaces, hindering reproducibility, fair comparison, and practical integration. In this paper, we present DataFlex, a unified data-centric dynamic training framework built upon LLaMA-Factory. DataFlex supports three major paradigms of dynamic data optimization: sample selection, domain mixture adjustment, and sample reweighting, while remaining fully compatible with the original training workflow. It provides extensible trainer abstractions and modular components, enabling a drop-in replacement for standard LLM training, and unifies key model-dependent operations such as embedding extraction, inference, and gradient computation, with support for large-scale settings including DeepSpeed ZeRO-3. We conduct comprehensive experiments across multiple data-centric methods. Dynamic data selection consistently outperforms static full-data training on MMLU across both Mistral-7B and Llama-3.2-3B. For data mixture, DoReMi and ODM improve both MMLU accuracy and corpus-level perplexity over default proportions when pretraining Qwen2.5-1.5B on SlimPajama at 6B and 30B token scales. DataFlex also achieves consistent runtime improvements over original implementations. These results demonstrate that DataFlex provides an effective, efficient, and reproducible infrastructure for data-centric dynamic training of LLMs.&quot;,&quot;upvotes&quot;:248,&quot;discussionId&quot;:&quot;69ccf51d1f6782218d973dd5&quot;,&quot;projectPage&quot;:&quot;https://opendcai.github.io/DataFlex-Doc/en/&quot;,&quot;githubRepo&quot;:&quot;https://github.com/OpenDCAI/DataFlex&quot;,&quot;githubRepoAddedBy&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;ai_summary&quot;:&quot;DataFlex is a unified framework for dynamic data-centric training of large language models that supports sample selection, domain mixture adjustment, and sample reweighting while maintaining compatibility with standard training workflows and enabling efficient large-scale deployment.&quot;,&quot;ai_keywords&quot;:[&quot;data-centric training&quot;,&quot;large language models&quot;,&quot;sample selection&quot;,&quot;domain mixture adjustment&quot;,&quot;sample reweighting&quot;,&quot;LLaMA-Factory&quot;,&quot;extensible trainer abstractions&quot;,&quot;modular components&quot;,&quot;embedding extraction&quot;,&quot;gradient computation&quot;,&quot;DeepSpeed ZeRO-3&quot;,&quot;MMLU&quot;,&quot;perplexity&quot;,&quot;Qwen2.5-1.5B&quot;,&quot;SlimPajama&quot;],&quot;ai_summary_model&quot;:&quot;Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct&quot;,&quot;githubStars&quot;:3487,&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;61dcd8e344f59573371b5cb6&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;PekingUniversity&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Peking University&quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/noauth/vavgrBsnkSejriUF4lXDE.png&quot;}},&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-03-27T04:28:02.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;DataFlex: A Unified Framework for Data-Centric Dynamic Training of Large Language Models&quot;,&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;Data-centric training has emerged as a promising direction for improving large language models (LLMs) by optimizing not only model parameters but also the selection, composition, and weighting of training data during optimization. However, existing approaches to data selection, data mixture optimization, and data reweighting are often developed in isolated codebases with inconsistent interfaces, hindering reproducibility, fair comparison, and practical integration. In this paper, we present DataFlex, a unified data-centric dynamic training framework built upon LLaMA-Factory. DataFlex supports three major paradigms of dynamic data optimization: sample selection, domain mixture adjustment, and sample reweighting, while remaining fully compatible with the original training workflow. It provides extensible trainer abstractions and modular components, enabling a drop-in replacement for standard LLM training, and unifies key model-dependent operations such as embedding extraction, inference, and gradient computation, with support for large-scale settings including DeepSpeed ZeRO-3. We conduct comprehensive experiments across multiple data-centric methods. Dynamic data selection consistently outperforms static full-data training on MMLU across both Mistral-7B and Llama-3.2-3B. For data mixture, DoReMi and ODM improve both MMLU accuracy and corpus-level perplexity over default proportions when pretraining Qwen2.5-1.5B on SlimPajama at 6B and 30B token scales. DataFlex also achieves consistent runtime improvements over original implementations. These results demonstrate that DataFlex provides an effective, efficient, and reproducible infrastructure for data-centric dynamic training of LLMs.&quot;,&quot;thumbnail&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-thumbnails.huggingface.co/social-thumbnails/papers/2603.26164.png&quot;,&quot;numComments&quot;:4,&quot;upvoted&quot;:false,&quot;submittedBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6671214c92412fd4640714eb&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/c1556168b703c9b87276fb679d044f61.svg&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Bohan Zeng&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;zbhpku&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;isHf&quot;:false,&quot;isHfAdmin&quot;:false,&quot;isMod&quot;:false,&quot;followerCount&quot;:16,&quot;isUserFollowing&quot;:false},&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;61dcd8e344f59573371b5cb6&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;PekingUniversity&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Peking University&quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/noauth/vavgrBsnkSejriUF4lXDE.png&quot;},&quot;isAuthorParticipating&quot;:true},{&quot;paper&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;2609.33439&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:[{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6abc7212d51a189976e024e4&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;EverMind AI&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false}],&quot;mediaUrls&quot;:[&quot;https://cdn-uploads.huggingface.co/production/uploads/661df0eeb3f414cc0af149c9/YvG-zgwbftmKvmsQxSRIf.jpeg&quot;],&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-09-27T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyAt&quot;:&quot;2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Raven: The Harness of Harnesses for Composable Agentic Intelligence&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;661df0eeb3f414cc0af149c9&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/no-auth/F2erCT0aMTByiinTdJCmC.png&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;LivXue&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;LivXue&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;LivXue&quot;},&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;As large language models advance, AI agents are moving beyond isolated, domain-specific tasks toward long-horizon, cross-domain workflows. This transition exposes two challenges: increasing harness complexity makes manual design difficult to scale, while tighter coupling to specific domains limits the generality of a single harness. The central question thus shifts from how to engineer a stronger harness for one domain to how to autonomously construct specialized harnesses, improve them through experience, and orchestrate them across domains. We introduce Raven, The Harness of Harnesses, an open-source multi-agent ecosystem that automatically constructs and evolves modular harnesses for specific models and domains, treating each executable model--harness pair as a composable unit of intelligence. To support an All-Domain Collaboration Network, its Host Agent decomposes goals, matches subtasks to specialized agents, coordinates execution dependencies, and integrates results, while a host archive and EverOS preserve experience across tasks and Skill Forge makes that experience available as reusable procedures. Our theory establishes sufficient conditions for such composition to expand reliable task coverage beyond that of the available individual agents under a shared resource budget. On complex and long-horizon tasks, Raven significantly outperforms the state-of-the-art agent systems, pushing the frontier of composable agentic intelligence.&quot;,&quot;upvotes&quot;:99,&quot;discussionId&quot;:&quot;6abc7213d51a189976e024e5&quot;,&quot;projectPage&quot;:&quot;https://raven.evermind.ai/&quot;,&quot;githubRepo&quot;:&quot;https://github.com/EverMind-AI/Raven&quot;,&quot;githubRepoAddedBy&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;ai_summary&quot;:&quot;Raven is an open-source multi-agent ecosystem that autonomously builds and evolves modular harnesses, enabling cross-domain collaboration and expanding reliable task coverage through composable agent units.&quot;,&quot;ai_keywords&quot;:[&quot;multi-agent ecosystem&quot;,&quot;modular harnesses&quot;,&quot;All-Domain Collaboration Network&quot;,&quot;Host Agent&quot;,&quot;EverOS&quot;,&quot;Skill Forge&quot;,&quot;composable agentic intelligence&quot;],&quot;ai_summary_model&quot;:&quot;thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small&quot;,&quot;githubStars&quot;:6103,&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;68c0e394d0a939784bb82a24&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;EverMindAI&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;EverMind&quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/68c0e2432d6dd107416d3f37/xkxLPRUJRIboDe1mClCqX.png&quot;}},&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-09-26T20:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Raven: The Harness of Harnesses for Composable Agentic Intelligence&quot;,&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;As large language models advance, AI agents are moving beyond isolated, domain-specific tasks toward long-horizon, cross-domain workflows. This transition exposes two challenges: increasing harness complexity makes manual design difficult to scale, while tighter coupling to specific domains limits the generality of a single harness. The central question thus shifts from how to engineer a stronger harness for one domain to how to autonomously construct specialized harnesses, improve them through experience, and orchestrate them across domains. We introduce Raven, The Harness of Harnesses, an open-source multi-agent ecosystem that automatically constructs and evolves modular harnesses for specific models and domains, treating each executable model--harness pair as a composable unit of intelligence. To support an All-Domain Collaboration Network, its Host Agent decomposes goals, matches subtasks to specialized agents, coordinates execution dependencies, and integrates results, while a host archive and EverOS preserve experience across tasks and Skill Forge makes that experience available as reusable procedures. Our theory establishes sufficient conditions for such composition to expand reliable task coverage beyond that of the available individual agents under a shared resource budget. On complex and long-horizon tasks, Raven significantly outperforms the state-of-the-art agent systems, pushing the frontier of composable agentic intelligence.&quot;,&quot;mediaUrls&quot;:[&quot;https://cdn-uploads.huggingface.co/production/uploads/661df0eeb3f414cc0af149c9/YvG-zgwbftmKvmsQxSRIf.jpeg&quot;],&quot;thumbnail&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-thumbnails.huggingface.co/social-thumbnails/papers/2609.33439.png&quot;,&quot;numComments&quot;:9,&quot;upvoted&quot;:false,&quot;submittedBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;661df0eeb3f414cc0af149c9&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/no-auth/F2erCT0aMTByiinTdJCmC.png&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;LivXue&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;LivXue&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;isHf&quot;:false,&quot;isHfAdmin&quot;:false,&quot;isMod&quot;:false,&quot;followerCount&quot;:3,&quot;isUserFollowing&quot;:false},&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;68c0e394d0a939784bb82a24&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;EverMindAI&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;EverMind&quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/68c0e2432d6dd107416d3f37/xkxLPRUJRIboDe1mClCqX.png&quot;},&quot;isAuthorParticipating&quot;:false},{&quot;paper&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;2611.03178&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:[{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8cc&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Jiajie Jin&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8cd&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;61cd4b833dd34ba1985e0753&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/61cd4b833dd34ba1985e0753/BfHfrwotoMESpXZOHiIe4.png&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;KABI&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;dongguanting&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;dongguanting&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Guanting Dong&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-11-03T09:48:58.349Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8ce&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Chengjun Pan&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8cf&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Xin Deng&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8d0&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zhuohui Sheng&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8d1&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Guoqiang Wang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8d2&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Tao Gui&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8d3&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Yutao Zhu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8d4&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Yujia Chen&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8d5&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Shihong Yi&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8d6&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Binze Hu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8d7&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zhixiong Yang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8d8&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zhichao Sun&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8d9&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Rui Wang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8da&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Han Han&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8db&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Mingyu Ma&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8dc&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Junhao Huang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8dd&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Xiaotao Wang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8de&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;679084bf7c5379ada9e11024&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/679084bf7c5379ada9e11024/F7Npmv4ZlUta4PayUZkhl.png&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Huicheng Jiang&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;tangerine6&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;tangerine6&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Huicheng Jiang&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-11-03T16:45:04.672Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b6