6e7072330a58301366.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Xiaoqian Zhang&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;zhangqiol&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;zhangqiol&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Xiaoqian Zhang&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-11-05T08:45:04.941Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8e7&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Yulun Zhu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8e8&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Xiaoxi Li&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8e9&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Jiahang Lin&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8ea&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Shaofan Liu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8eb&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Shihan Dou&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8ec&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zhiheng Xi&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8ed&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Qi Zhang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8ee&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Yu-Gang Jiang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8ef&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;See-Kiong Ng&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8f0&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Yang Zhang&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8f1&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Tat-Seng Chua&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8f2&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ji-Rong Wen&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6ae9932b4b63b3479c38a8f3&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zhicheng Dou&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false}],&quot;mediaUrls&quot;:[&quot;https://cdn-uploads.huggingface.co/production/uploads/61cd4b833dd34ba1985e0753/MtYdVA_zvSVOUJqPXPO_3.mp4&quot;],&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-11-02T14:15:11.000Z&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyAt&quot;:&quot;2026-11-03T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;CoworkOS:Scaling Agent Coworkers for Real-world Automation&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;61cd4b833dd34ba1985e0753&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/61cd4b833dd34ba1985e0753/BfHfrwotoMESpXZOHiIe4.png&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;KABI&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;dongguanting&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;dongguanting&quot;},&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;Rapid advances in cowork agents are shifting human-AI collaboration toward real-world automation, delivering software, designs, and other artifacts. However, such productivity work demands both high-quality delivery on complex productivity tasks and continued monitoring and decision-making over long horizons, a combination that remains an open challenge. We introduce CoworkOS, a general-purpose harness for long-horizon work that separates task strategy from execution management: the model decides actions, delegation, and acceptance, while the runtime maintains state and feedback. Its three-layer architecture enables direct execution or delegation to Subagents, synchronously or asynchronously, under stable responsibilities. Through a shared application layer, humans and agents inspect and revise the same evolving documents, presentations, CAD models, and Blender scenes, so human-in-the-loop participation can enter both through conversation and through direct modification of the work itself. To sustain continuity across agents and sessions, CoworkOS further introduces hierarchical workspaces and persistent semantic memory, so working files, key decisions, and long-running Job logs remain shareable, reusable, and resumable after interruption. Across 12 benchmarks and 6 categories of real-world applications, CoworkOS proves highly competitive with frontier agent applications such as Codex and DeepSeek Harness. As a sustained-work case study, CoworkOS uses GLM-5.3 as its backbone to conduct RSI-driven automated post-training on Qwen3.6-35B-A3B. Over five rounds, the model's average score across eight benchmarks rose from 33.19 to 42.95 (+9.76). Looking ahead, we believe CoworkOS opens a meaningful path toward general cowork-agent intelligence.&quot;,&quot;upvotes&quot;:100,&quot;discussionId&quot;:&quot;6ae9932c4b63b3479c38a8f4&quot;,&quot;projectPage&quot;:&quot;https://coworkos-ai.github.io&quot;,&quot;githubRepo&quot;:&quot;https://github.com/RUC-NLPIR/CoworkOS&quot;,&quot;githubRepoAddedBy&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;ai_summary&quot;:&quot;CoworkOS is a long-horizon agent harness that separates strategy from execution, supports human-in-the-loop collaboration via shared artifacts, and improves model performance through sustained automated post-training.&quot;,&quot;ai_keywords&quot;:[&quot;cowork agents&quot;,&quot;long-horizon work&quot;,&quot;Subagents&quot;,&quot;hierarchical workspaces&quot;,&quot;persistent semantic memory&quot;,&quot;human-in-the-loop&quot;,&quot;automated post-training&quot;],&quot;ai_summary_model&quot;:&quot;thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small&quot;,&quot;githubStars&quot;:142,&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;622177ac43826d6f261f8208&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;RUC&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Renmin University of China&quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/61ac8f8a00d01045fca0ad2f/670IAX9A2-BflqA5MiSBW.jpeg&quot;}},&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-11-02T09:15:11.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;CoworkOS:Scaling Agent Coworkers for Real-world Automation&quot;,&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;Rapid advances in cowork agents are shifting human-AI collaboration toward real-world automation, delivering software, designs, and other artifacts. However, such productivity work demands both high-quality delivery on complex productivity tasks and continued monitoring and decision-making over long horizons, a combination that remains an open challenge. We introduce CoworkOS, a general-purpose harness for long-horizon work that separates task strategy from execution management: the model decides actions, delegation, and acceptance, while the runtime maintains state and feedback. Its three-layer architecture enables direct execution or delegation to Subagents, synchronously or asynchronously, under stable responsibilities. Through a shared application layer, humans and agents inspect and revise the same evolving documents, presentations, CAD models, and Blender scenes, so human-in-the-loop participation can enter both through conversation and through direct modification of the work itself. To sustain continuity across agents and sessions, CoworkOS further introduces hierarchical workspaces and persistent semantic memory, so working files, key decisions, and long-running Job logs remain shareable, reusable, and resumable after interruption. Across 12 benchmarks and 6 categories of real-world applications, CoworkOS proves highly competitive with frontier agent applications such as Codex and DeepSeek Harness. As a sustained-work case study, CoworkOS uses GLM-5.3 as its backbone to conduct RSI-driven automated post-training on Qwen3.6-35B-A3B. Over five rounds, the model's average score across eight benchmarks rose from 33.19 to 42.95 (+9.76). Looking ahead, we believe CoworkOS opens a meaningful path toward general cowork-agent intelligence.&quot;,&quot;mediaUrls&quot;:[&quot;https://cdn-uploads.huggingface.co/production/uploads/61cd4b833dd34ba1985e0753/MtYdVA_zvSVOUJqPXPO_3.mp4&quot;],&quot;thumbnail&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-thumbnails.huggingface.co/social-thumbnails/papers/2611.03178.png&quot;,&quot;numComments&quot;:4,&quot;upvoted&quot;:false,&quot;submittedBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;61cd4b833dd34ba1985e0753&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/61cd4b833dd34ba1985e0753/BfHfrwotoMESpXZOHiIe4.png&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;KABI&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;dongguanting&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;isHf&quot;:false,&quot;isHfAdmin&quot;:false,&quot;isMod&quot;:false,&quot;followerCount&quot;:97,&quot;isUserFollowing&quot;:false},&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;622177ac43826d6f261f8208&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;RUC&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Renmin University of China&quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/61ac8f8a00d01045fca0ad2f/670IAX9A2-BflqA5MiSBW.jpeg&quot;},&quot;isAuthorParticipating&quot;:true},{&quot;paper&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;2610.14162&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:[{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aceeac3abe004a210f25934&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Hermann Kumbong&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aceeac3abe004a210f25935&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;65d7c02de70515f9a23c5bba&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/ee79da9d78b8dacba112df018e43f710.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:true,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Ishan Khare&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;iskhare&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;iskhare&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ishan S. Khare&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;claimed_verified&quot;,&quot;statusLastChangedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-16T08:34:15.035Z&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aceeac3abe004a210f25936&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Iddah Mlauzi&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aceeac3abe004a210f25937&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Andrew Woen&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aceeac3abe004a210f25938&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Charles Ding&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aceeac3abe004a210f25939&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;E. Kelly Buchanan&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aceeac3abe004a210f2593a&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Simran Arora&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aceeac3abe004a210f2593b&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Azalia Mirhoseini&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6aceeac3abe004a210f2593c&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Christopher Ré&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false}],&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-15T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6525fd79e0094b7bf21c01e6&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/b652032b988b1c8b3fc7e085c886bd70.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:true,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Hermann Kumbong&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;kumboh&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;kumboh&quot;},&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;Diffusion language models (DLMs) offer parallel sampling for faster generation than autoregressive models, an increasingly important advantage as inference becomes a dominant computational workload. However, DLMs degrade quickly with fewer sampling steps, process the full sequence at every step, and require many passes over the dataset to reach good quality. We introduce Next-Concept Modeling (NCM), a two-stage, coarse-to-fine framework: a multiscale residual VQ-VAE encodes text into a hierarchy of discrete codes, and a transformer generates one level at a time, predicting all codes within a level in parallel. At matched parameter scales, NCM achieves better generative perplexity than the strongest DLM baseline on LM1B while running 21times faster. On OpenWebText, NCM is competitive with the strongest DLM while running 10times faster; on XSum, it matches the strongest DLM's ROUGE-L while being 31times faster. On the reasoning task of Sudoku, NCM outperforms autoregressive and diffusion baselines across all difficulty levels, using fewer function evaluations. On the reasoning task of Sudoku, NCM outperforms autoregressive and diffusion baselines across all difficulty levels, using fewer function evaluations.&quot;,&quot;upvotes&quot;:23,&quot;discussionId&quot;:&quot;6aceeac4abe004a210f2593d&quot;,&quot;projectPage&quot;:&quot;https://hazyresearch.stanford.edu/blog/2026-10-12-ncm&quot;,&quot;githubRepo&quot;:&quot;https://github.com/HazyResearch/ncm&quot;,&quot;githubRepoAddedBy&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;ai_summary&quot;:&quot;Next-Concept Modeling uses hierarchical discrete codes and parallel level-wise generation to accelerate diffusion language models while improving quality and reasoning performance.&quot;,&quot;ai_keywords&quot;:[&quot;diffusion language models&quot;,&quot;parallel sampling&quot;,&quot;multiscale residual VQ-VAE&quot;,&quot;discrete codes&quot;,&quot;transformer&quot;,&quot;generative perplexity&quot;,&quot;function evaluations&quot;],&quot;ai_summary_model&quot;:&quot;thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small&quot;,&quot;githubStars&quot;:1505,&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;672c672dcf09d152f4da04c4&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;StanfordUniversity&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Stanford University&quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/68e396f2b5bb631e9b2fac9a/vJI0POlzGMXL2878t1vz2.jpeg&quot;}},&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-10-08T20:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Next-Concept Modeling: Fast, Parallel Coarse-to-Fine Text Generation&quot;,&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;Diffusion language models (DLMs) offer parallel sampling for faster generation than autoregressive models, an increasingly important advantage as inference becomes a dominant computational workload. However, DLMs degrade quickly with fewer sampling steps, process the full sequence at every step, and require many passes over the dataset to reach good quality. We introduce Next-Concept Modeling (NCM), a two-stage, coarse-to-fine framework: a multiscale residual VQ-VAE encodes text into a hierarchy of discrete codes, and a transformer generates one level at a time, predicting all codes within a level in parallel. At matched parameter scales, NCM achieves better generative perplexity than the strongest DLM baseline on LM1B while running 21times faster. On OpenWebText, NCM is competitive with the strongest DLM while running 10times faster; on XSum, it matches the strongest DLM's ROUGE-L while being 31times faster. On the reasoning task of Sudoku, NCM outperforms autoregressive and diffusion baselines across all difficulty levels, using fewer function evaluations. On the reasoning task of Sudoku, NCM outperforms autoregressive and diffusion baselines across all difficulty levels, using fewer function evaluations.&quot;,&quot;thumbnail&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-thumbnails.huggingface.co/social-thumbnails/papers/2610.14162.png&quot;,&quot;numComments&quot;:2,&quot;upvoted&quot;:false,&quot;submittedBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6525fd79e0094b7bf21c01e6&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/b652032b988b1c8b3fc7e085c886bd70.svg&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Hermann Kumbong&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;kumboh&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:true,&quot;isHf&quot;:false,&quot;isHfAdmin&quot;:false,&quot;isMod&quot;:false,&quot;followerCount&quot;:1,&quot;isUserFollowing&quot;:false},&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;672c672dcf09d152f4da04c4&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;StanfordUniversity&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Stanford University&quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/68e396f2b5bb631e9b2fac9a/vJI0POlzGMXL2878t1vz2.jpeg&quot;},&quot;isAuthorParticipating&quot;:false},{&quot;paper&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;2605.31264&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:[{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6a1cf553808ddbc3c7d434af&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Tianyi Zhou&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6a1cf553808ddbc3c7d434b0&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Dongrui Liu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6a1cf553808ddbc3c7d434b1&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Leitao Yuan&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6a1cf553808ddbc3c7d434b2&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Jing Shao&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false},{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6a1cf553808ddbc3c7d434b3&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Xia Hu&quot;,&quot;hidden&quot;:false}],&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-05-29T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyAt&quot;:&quot;2026-06-01T00:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;COLLEAGUE.SKILL: Automated AI Skill Generation via Expert Knowledge Distillation&quot;,&quot;submittedOnDailyBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;66e2624a436a1798365e4581&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/263a1533f1183499a88ae9581b00dc2f.svg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Qihan Ren&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;jasonrqh&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;jasonrqh&quot;},&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;LLM agents are increasingly expected not only to complete isolated tasks, but also to carry bounded representations of human expertise, judgment, and interaction style. Building such person-grounded agents remains difficult because actionable knowledge associated with a person or role is usually embedded in heterogeneous traces rather than written as clean instructions. Existing memory and persona systems capture fragments of this evidence, while skill frameworks provide portable packaging formats; however, there is no end-to-end workflow for distilling these traces into inspectable, correctable, and agent-usable skills. We present an automated trace-to-skill distillation system for generating person-grounded AI skills via expert knowledge distillation. Given materials from a target person or role, COLLEAGUE.SKILL produces a versioned skill package with two coordinated tracks: a capability track for practices, mental models, and decision heuristics, and a bounded behavior track for communication style, interaction rules, and correction history. The package can be inspected, invoked, updated through natural-language feedback, rolled back, installed across agent hosts, and optionally prepared for controlled distribution. We describe the artifact contract, generation workflow, correction lifecycle, deployment surface, and domain presets implemented in the open-source system. At the time of writing, the public repository has approximately 18.5k GitHub stars; the gallery lists 215 skills from 165 contributors and more than 100k cumulative stars across listed skill cards. The system illustrates how person-grounded skills can be represented as portable, correctable packages rather than opaque prompts or hidden memories.&quot;,&quot;upvotes&quot;:130,&quot;discussionId&quot;:&quot;6a1cf554808ddbc3c7d434b4&quot;,&quot;githubRepo&quot;:&quot;https://github.com/titanwings/colleague-skill&quot;,&quot;githubRepoAddedBy&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;ai_summary&quot;:&quot;Person-grounded AI skills are automatically distilled from heterogeneous traces into inspectable, correctable packages that capture both capabilities and behavioral patterns.&quot;,&quot;ai_keywords&quot;:[&quot;expert knowledge distillation&quot;,&quot;person-grounded agents&quot;,&quot;trace-to-skill distillation&quot;,&quot;capability track&quot;,&quot;behavior track&quot;,&quot;skill package&quot;,&quot;correction lifecycle&quot;,&quot;deployment surface&quot;,&quot;domain presets&quot;],&quot;ai_summary_model&quot;:&quot;Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct&quot;,&quot;githubStars&quot;:26427,&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6747ee5decec679eafb90450&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ShanghaiAiLab&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;shanghai ailab &quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/6cd2acf412ad103653d9ce14a1aacc19?d=retro&amp;size=100&quot;}},&quot;publishedAt&quot;:&quot;2026-05-28T20:00:00.000Z&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;COLLEAGUE.SKILL: Automated AI Skill Generation via Expert Knowledge Distillation&quot;,&quot;summary&quot;:&quot;LLM agents are increasingly expected not only to complete isolated tasks, but also to carry bounded representations of human expertise, judgment, and interaction style. Building such person-grounded agents remains difficult because actionable knowledge associated with a person or role is usually embedded in heterogeneous traces rather than written as clean instructions. Existing memory and persona systems capture fragments of this evidence, while skill frameworks provide portable packaging formats; however, there is no end-to-end workflow for distilling these traces into inspectable, correctable, and agent-usable skills. We present an automated trace-to-skill distillation system for generating person-grounded AI skills via expert knowledge distillation. Given materials from a target person or role, COLLEAGUE.SKILL produces a versioned skill package with two coordinated tracks: a capability track for practices, mental models, and decision heuristics, and a bounded behavior track for communication style, interaction rules, and correction history. The package can be inspected, invoked, updated through natural-language feedback, rolled back, installed across agent hosts, and optionally prepared for controlled distribution. We describe the artifact contract, generation workflow, correction lifecycle, deployment surface, and domain presets implemented in the open-source system. At the time of writing, the public repository has approximately 18.5k GitHub stars; the gallery lists 215 skills from 165 contributors and more than 100k cumulative stars across listed skill cards. The system illustrates how person-grounded skills can be represented as portable, correctable packages rather than opaque prompts or hidden memories.&quot;,&quot;thumbnail&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-thumbnails.huggingface.co/social-thumbnails/papers/2605.31264.png&quot;,&quot;numComments&quot;:3,&quot;upvoted&quot;:false,&quot;submittedBy&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;66e2624a436a1798365e4581&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;/avatars/263a1533f1183499a88ae9581b00dc2f.svg&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;Qihan Ren&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;jasonrqh&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;isHf&quot;:false,&quot;isHfAdmin&quot;:false,&quot;isMod&quot;:false,&quot;followerCount&quot;:11,&quot;isUserFollowing&quot;:false},&quot;organization&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;6747ee5decec679eafb90450&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ShanghaiAiLab&quot;,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;shanghai ailab &quot;,&quot;avatar&quot;:&quot;https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/6cd2acf412ad103653d9ce14a1aacc19?d=retro&amp;size=100&quot;},&quot;isAuthorParticipating&quot;:false}],&quot;publisher&quot;:{&quot;_id&quot;:&quot;60f1abe7544c2adfd699860c&quot;,&quot;avatarUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/1674929746905-60f1abe7544c2adfd699860c.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isPro&quot;:false,&quot;fullname&quot;:&quot;AK&quot;,&quot;user&quot;:&quot;akhaliq&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;},&quot;query&quot;:{},&quot;isTrending&quot;:true}"><section class="container relative mb-20 mt-8 md:mt-14"><div class="mb-8 grid grid-cols-6 items-start md:mb-12 md:grid-cols-12 md:gap-x-4"><div class="order-1 col-span-5 md:order-none md:col-span-10 lg:col-span-8 xl:col-span-4 xl:pl-0"><div class="flex items-center gap-3"><h1 class="text-2xl font-bold md:text-3xl">Trending Papers</h1> <!--[-1--><!--]--></div> <h2 class="whitespace-nowrap text-gray-500 xl:text-lg">by<a href="/akhaliq"><img alt="" class="mx-1.5 inline h-4" src="/front/assets/papers-by.png"/><span class="underline">AK</span></a> and the research community</h2></div> <div class="order-1 col-span-1 flex justify-end pt-1 md:order-none md:col-span-2 md:mt-0 lg:col-span-4 xl:h