t"/></div><!----></a><!--]--> <!--[0--><div class="shadow-xs pointer-events-none absolute bottom-2 right-2 flex h-6 items-center gap-1 whitespace-nowrap rounded-md border bg-white px-2 text-xs leading-none text-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-900 dark:text-gray-400">Submitted by <div class="flex-none  "><img alt="" loading="lazy" class="max-w-none size-2.5 rounded-full  flex-none select-none " src="/avatars/ada8828dbed3b49cb202a7945046b85f.svg" crossorigin="anonymous"/> <!--[-1--><!--]--></div><!----> andy-yang</div><!--]--></div> <div class="from-gray-50-to-white bg-linear-to-b flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col justify-center p-6"><h3 class="mb-1.5 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 hover:underline dark:text-white"><a href="/papers/2608.16157" class="line-clamp-2 cursor-pointer text-balance">FreeToken: Efficient Edge-Native MoE Serving with Bandwidth-Adaptive Execution</a></h3> <!--[0--><div class="mb-2"><p class="line-clamp-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">FreeToken is an edge-native Mixture-of-Experts serving system that dynamically maps computation and model state onto heterogeneous local hardware to run large open-weight models on personal machines.</p></div><!--]--> <div class="flex min-w-0 items-center text-sm text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-500"><!--[0--><a href="/UCBerkeley" class="inline-flex min-w-0 max-w-full items-center rounded-full border border-blue-200/70 bg-blue-50 py-0.5 text-blue-700 hover:border-blue-200 hover:bg-blue-100 dark:border-blue-500/20 dark:bg-blue-900/30 dark:text-blue-300 dark:hover:border-blue-500/30 dark:hover:bg-blue-900/50 px-1.5 text-xs gap-1 "><!--[0--><img src="https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/63f425c3a096536aeab42dea/bxNKEkprdm5JI1wkjmNAL.png" alt="UCBerkeley" class="size-3 rounded-sm"/><!--]--> <span class="block min-w-0 truncate font-medium">University of California, Berkeley</span></a><!--]--> <!--[0--><span class="mx-2">·</span> <span>Published on Aug 17, 2026</span><!--]--></div></div> <div class="from-